Aug 15, 2025

Stranded Rossi Peaks were generated by merging two datasets from the Rossi paper. 

1. Their github contains the (A) set of peak calls for each TF (merged by replicate). 
   https://github.com/CEGRcode/2021-Rossi_Nature/tree/master/04_ChExMix_Peaks
2. Next, their ftp site contains the individual replicate TF experiments. In each experiment, MEME was called and a set of motifs were identified. For each motif, the MEME hit contained the stranded information is identified.
   https://www.datacommons.psu.edu/download/eberly/pughlab/yeast-epigenome-project/

Our process for merging: 
1. For each transcription factor, download the individual replication files containing the motif matches.
2. For each replicate,
3. For each motif, cross reference the peak calls (A) with the motif matches. If the peak call is inside the motif, create an entry containing the strand information, the replicate, and the motif,
4. Following completion of 2-3, merge the stranded peak call hits into a single bed file.
5. Perform this for all TFs and create bed files

